WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.633
ResNet.

2
00:00:01.933 --> 00:00:05.372
Before 2015, going deeper made networks worse.

3
00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.867
One idea fixed that.

4
00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:11.233
Past about twenty conv layers, plain stacks got worse.

5
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:15.066
Not from overfitting, but because they were hard to optimize.

6
00:00:15.066 --> 00:00:18.367
The error signal degrades through every layer it crosses.

7
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:20.600
Here's the fix.

8
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.633
The block takes an input, x.

9
00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:25.433
The layers compute a correction, F of x.

10
00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:29.500
And a skip connection adds the original input back to the output.

11
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.733
As an equation.

12
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:36.000
The block only has to learn the residual, the correction to the identity.

13
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.467
The skip carries the input through untouched.

14
00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:42.967
So learning change nothing is easy, and extra depth can no longer hurt.

15
00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.133
The deeper reason is the gradient.

16
00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:48.900
At the addition, backprop's signal splits.

17
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:55.467
One copy flows straight through the skip, unmodified, bypassing every multiplication that could shrink it.

18
00:00:55.767 --> 00:01:01.400
That took depth from twenty layers to over a hundred and fifty, and reappears in every transformer.

19
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.433
In practice, you fine-tune a pretrained ResNet.

20
00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:08.667
Load ResNet eighteen with its ImageNet weights.

21
00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:10.900
Freeze every pretrained parameter.

22
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.000
Replace only the final layer with a two-class head.

23
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.633
And train just that head.

24
00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:17.900
Here's the payoff.

25
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.700
You have two thousand labeled satellite tiles, hopeless for training a deep CNN from scratch.

26
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.033
But the pretrained backbone already knows edges, textures, and shapes.

27
00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:35.257
Freeze, replace the head, train five epochs: about ninety four percent, versus seventy eight from scratch.

28
00:01:35.257 --> 00:01:38.000
It's the template for LLM fine-tuning too.

29
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.008
Let's recap.

30
00:01:40.008 --> 00:01:42.633
Plain deep stacks are hard to optimize.

31
00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:45.700
Skip connections compute F of x plus x.

32
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.667
They give gradients a highway back to the first layer.

33
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:53.228
And pretrained ResNets are the default for custom vision.

34
00:01:53.228 --> 00:01:54.200
Next up: VGG.
